&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;---@alias ngx.balancer.failure&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;---| &amp;#34;next&amp;#34; # Failures due to bad status codes sent from the backend server. The origin&amp;#39;s response is same though, which means the backend connection can still be reused for future requests.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;---| &amp;#34;failed&amp;#34; # Fatal errors while communicating to the backend server (like connection timeouts, connection resets, and etc). In this case, the backend connection must be aborted and cannot get reused.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
